          "worked": "Take natural logarithms and use the power law.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\ln(a^x)&=\\ln(b)\\\\x\\ln(a)&=\\ln(b)\\\\x&=\\frac{\\ln(b)}{\\ln(a)}\\end{align*}$$",
